          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "8dd05a11b6d962ed44f8bbccdaefeef8b94d96cde966e9d70b24ce8df59fb7cf"
          },
          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "4.3",
            "strix_vuln_class_hash": "dceef82e012d648b6ffca67b0c1234436b19d1ef6559276d2b7f1f5041ee5d7a",
            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0001",
              "severity": "medium",
              "cvss": 4.3,
              "timestamp": "2026-08-23 03:20:39 UTC",
              "target": "http://host.docker.internal:3123",
              "endpoint": "/socket.io/",
              "method": "WebSocket",
              "cwe": "CWE-602",
              "impact": "A low-privilege player can deterministically win any hosted competitive **`cups`** round by forging a perfect final submission before the natural shuffle sequence finishes. This causes unauthorized leaderboard manipulation and score inflation in live rooms; in the validated two-player proof of concept, the cheater received **`5500 pts`** / **`1000`** normalized points while the honest player received **`0 pts`**.",
              "technical_analysis": "The competitive-room guard in `server/room.js` does not disable **`cups`**, so hosted sessions can still queue a minigame whose scoring is fully client-derivable.\n\n```javascript title=server/room.js startLineNumber=41 endLineNumber=50\nconst COMPETITIVE_CLIENT_SCORING_DISABLED = new Set([\n  'trace', 'stopclock', 'slingshot', 'balance',\n  'oddoneout', 'typing', 'spacemash',\n]);\n\nfunction clientScoredGameAllowed(room, key) {\n  return room.solo || room.allowClientScoredCompetitive || !COMPETITIVE_CLIENT_SCORING_DISABLED.has(key);\n}\n```\n\nWhen **`cups`** is built, the server sends a public `seed`, `maxLevels`, and `baseCups` to every player. No server-only secret is retained for answer validation.\n\n```javascript title=server/games.js startLineNumber=361 endLineNumber=378\ncase 'cups': {\n  return {\n    clientData: {\n      seed: `cups-${Math.floor(rng() * 1e9)}`,\n      maxLevels: CUPS_MAX_LEVELS,\n      baseCups: CUPS_BASE_CUPS,\n    },\n    secret: {},\n  };\n}\n```\n\nThe shared implementation in `shared/cups.js` deterministically derives the correct `ball` location for every level from that public seed.\n\n```javascript title=shared/cups.js startLineNumber=58 endLineNumber=85\nexport function cupsLevel(seed, level, { baseCups = CUPS_BASE_CUPS, maxCups = CUPS_MAX_CUPS } = {}) {\n  const n = Math.max(1, Math.floor(level));\n  const rng = seededRng(`${seed}:lvl${n}`);\n  const cups = cupsCount(n, baseCups, maxCups);\n  const swapCount = 2 + n;\n  const swapMs = cupsSwapMs(n);\n  const allPairs = pairsFor(cups);\n\n  const start = randInt(rng, 0, cups - 1);\n  const swaps = [];\n  let ball = start;\n  let prev = null;\n  for (let i = 0; i < swapCount; i++) {\n    const choices = prev ? allPairs.filter((p) => !(p.a === prev.a && p.b === prev.b)) : allPairs;\n    const swap = choices[randInt(rng, 0, choices.length - 1)];\n    swaps.push(swap);\n    if (ball === swap.a) ball = swap.b;\n    else if (ball === swap.b) ball = swap.a;\n    prev = swap;\n  }\n\n  return { level: n, cups, start, swaps, swapMs, ball, shuffleMs: swaps.length * swapMs };\n}\n```\n\nAt submission time, `Room.handleSubmit()` stores the client payload and immediately scores it with `computeMetric('cups')` without requiring authoritative per-level interaction data. The cups scorer accepts a one-shot `payload.picks` array and awards **`100 * level`** for each correct forged entry.\n\n```javascript title=server/room.js startLineNumber=954 endLineNumber=978\nhandleSubmit(playerId, payload) {\n  if (this.phase !== 'minigame') return;\n  const p = this.players.get(playerId);\n  if (!p) return;\n  const g = this.round.games[this.round.gameIndex];\n  if (!g || g.submissions.has(playerId)) return;\n  g.submissions.set(playerId, payload ?? {});\n  if (!NEEDS_AGGREGATION.has(g.key)) {\n    let scoringPayload = payload;\n    if (PER_TURN_SECRET.has(g.key)) {\n      const locked = this.lockedSolved(g, playerId);\n      if (locked) scoringPayload = { ...(payload && typeof payload === 'object' ? payload : {}), solved: locked };\n    }\n    const metric = computeMetric(g.key, scoringPayload, g.secret, g.clientData, this.config);\n    if (metric != null) g.metrics.set(playerId, metric);\n  }\n  const total = this.players.size;\n  const submitted = g.submissions.size;\n  this.emitAll('host:progress', { submitted, total });\n  this.emitPlayer(playerId, 'submit:ack', { gameIndex: this.round.gameIndex });\n  if (submitted >= total) this.closeGame(g.token);\n}\n```\n\n```javascript title=server/games.js startLineNumber=799 endLineNumber=828\ncase 'cups': {\n  if (!Array.isArray(payload.picks)) return null;\n  const { seed, maxLevels, baseCups } = clientData;\n  let score = 0;\n  const n = Math.min(payload.picks.length, maxLevels);\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n    const level = i + 1;\n    const entry = payload.picks[i];\n    if (!entry || typeof entry !== 'object') continue;\n    if (entry.level !== level) continue;\n    const plan = cupsLevel(seed, level, { baseCups });\n    const idx = entry.cupIndex;\n    if (!Number.isInteger(idx) || idx < 0 || idx >= plan.cups) continue;\n    if (idx === plan.ball) score += 100 * level;\n  }\n  return score;\n}\n```\n\nBecause the server already tells the client everything required to compute `plan.ball`, a malicious player can emit a perfect final payload immediately after the `phase` event and beat the intended **`18336ms`** human-visible shuffle sequence by several orders of magnitude.",
              "remediation_steps": "1. Add **`cups`** to `COMPETITIVE_CLIENT_SCORING_DISABLED` so hosted competitive sessions cannot queue it.\n2. Keep `startTest('cups')` and solo practice unchanged so the minigame remains available for local testing and unscored practice.\n3. Before re-enabling **`cups`** competitively, redesign scoring so the server derives results from authoritative interaction data instead of trusting a one-shot client summary payload.",
              "poc": {
                "description": "1. Connect three Socket.IO clients to the application: one host, one attacker, and one honest player.\n2. Create a hosted room, configure the room so only **`cups`** is enabled, and join both players.\n3. Start the room and wait for the attacker to receive the `phase` event for the **`cups`** minigame.\n4. Read `clientData.seed`, `clientData.maxLevels`, and `clientData.baseCups` from that event.\n5. For each level from `1` to `maxLevels`, derive the correct final cup with the same `cupsLevel(seed, level, clientData)` logic used by the application and build `payload.picks` as `[{ level, cupIndex: plan.ball }, ...]`.\n6. Immediately emit `player:submit` with the synthesized payload, without waiting for the level shuffles to complete.\n7. Submit intentionally wrong picks for the honest player to show contrast.\n8. Observe that the server acknowledges the forged submission within a few milliseconds and awards the attacker the maximum **`5500 pts`** / **`1000`** normalized points.",
                "script_available": true
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-841",
          "ruleIndex": 1,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Late-joining player can enter the musical-chairs finale and win the session\n\nThe realtime room flow accepts a fresh **`player:join`** during the last queued competitive minigame. Because the musical-chairs finale then seeds participants from **all current room players**, the late entrant can skip the regular game, compete for the **3000-point** finale bonus, and still win the overall session."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "server/room.js"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 389,
                  "endLine": 396,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "if (this.phase !== 'lobby' && this.phase !== 'minigame') {\n      // Fresh players may join during the lobby or an active minigame (the\n      // issue #54 late-join feature: they score 0 for missed games and play\n      // the rest). Joining once the queue is exhausted — scores, the chairs\n      // finale, redemption, or the winner reveal — would let a stranger sit\n      // into the finale and change the outcome (Strix re-scan 2026-08-23).\n      return { error: 'Room is no longer accepting new players.' };\n    }"
                  }
                }
              },
              "message": {
                "text": "Reject fresh joins once the current minigame is the last queued competitive game"
              }
            },
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "server/room.js"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1135,
                  "endLine": 1143,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "startChairsFinale() {\n    this.round = null;\n    const ids = [...this.players.keys()];\n    this.chairs = {\n      active: ids,              // still holding a chair\n      eliminated: [],           // elimination order: first out first\n      totalRounds: Math.max(1, ids.length - 1),\n      round: 0,\n    };"
                  }
                }
              },
              "message": {
                "text": "Bonus finale currently seeds participants from all current room players"
              }
            },
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "/socket.io/",
